        "cost_usd": 0.1277385,
        "findings": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe new mapping follows the file's established idiom (inline `@Mapping` expressions alongside `membershipNumber` and `membershipLevel`), and the OpenAPI addition is placed and documented consistently. The one structural issue is duplication:\n\n- **Duplicated \"email present\" predicate.** The expression `owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank()` now appears verbatim in two mappings \u2014 the new `contactPreference` and the existing `membershipLevel`. This is the single concept \"the owner has an email\" copied inline in two places, so a future change to what counts as a present email (e.g. trimming, format check) has to be made in both spots or they silently drift.\n\n  Suggested fix: extract a `default boolean hasEmail(Owner owner)` on the interface and reference it from both expressions, e.g. `expression = \"java(hasEmail(owner) ? \\\"EMAIL\\\" : \\\"PHONE\\\")\"` and the corresponding term in `membershipLevel`. This keeps the inline-expression style the file already uses while giving the predicate one home and a name that states intent."
